\fBmkdir(path, options)\fR
Asynchronously creates a directory.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string; required) The path to create
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; optional) The optional options argument can be an integer specifying mode (permission and sticky bits), or an object with a mode property and a recursive property indicating whether parent directories should be created. Calling fs.mkdir() when path is a directory that exists results in an error only when recursive is false.
.br
\fIoptions.recursive\fR (boolean; optional; default false) Recursively create missing path segments.
.br
\fIoptions.mode\fR (number; optional; default 0o777) Set the mode of directory, or missing path segments when recursive is true.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise\fR Upon success, fulfills with undefined if recursive is false, or the first directory path created if recursive is true.
